From 8de720cca052a8c806a58e217b87787b68ae3ee2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 19 Nov 2026 06:47:41 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] kanban chat waits: owner-only subscriber check, root
 session stores, system notes never answer

Third review and adversarial pass of #3647:
- The subscriber check ran on the parking gateway. A pool worker parking a hub
  card has neither the hub's notify subscriptions (machine-local) nor its
  session stores, so every chat wait from a worker was refused. It now runs
  only where the card is owned (own_gateway == created_on, or an unsynced
  board); elsewhere the park records the ask, which syncs to the owner.
- tui_chat_reachable read stores under the caller's HERMES_HOME; a named-
  profile worker (HERMES_HOME=<root>/profiles/<name>) never saw the launch
  store. It now reads the root store and every profile store, as the sweeper.
- The chat probe's --after-id was taken before the park's own 'kanban-park'
  progress comment, which then fired it. `wait-comment --skip-system` ignores
  kernel writers (authors kanban-*), and the chat probe uses it; existing
  probes are unchanged.

Tests: the progress note and a dispatcher note do not fire the probe, an
answer does (schedule and block); foreign card parks and asks without a local
subscriber; owned card still needs one; named-profile worker sees the root
store chat. 6 of 47 fail on the previous head; 34 neighbouring files,
625 tests pass.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
